invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_message.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: the webpki hello lists x25519 but carries the hybrid share alone, so
  a server without the hybrid answers with a HelloRetryRequest naming
  x25519, which this client refuses as a group it already shared, and the
  handshake with a classic server fails instead of taking one round trip.
  docs/decisions.md entry 53 sends a share for x25519 and the hybrid, the
  two groups the hello lists ahead of secp256r1.

--- old
        if (!cfg->require_pq) {
            wb_u16(w, CH_GROUP_X25519);
            wb_u16(w, 32);
--- new
        if (0) {
            wb_u16(w, CH_GROUP_X25519);
            wb_u16(w, 32);
